course: dictionary
lesson: 5647
title: Reading about a lionfish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can work out a new word by reading the words around it. In «Lionfish have venomous spines and hunt small fish», the word lionfish is a kind of fish. The clues «venomous spines» and «hunt small fish» tell you what it does.
explain: «Bright colours on a reef often mean the opposite of hiding: a lionfish with spread fins is saying keep away.» The bright stripes are not hiding the fish. They are a warning, so the fish is saying "don't come near me."
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. Then try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are probably right.
explain: «Divers hunt them and chefs cook them to help reefs» shows that lionfish can cause problems far from their home seas. When the clues are not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: A lionfish is a striped red, brown and white sea fish.
fact: Lionfish have long fan-like fins and venomous spines, and the spines can give a very painful sting.
fact: Lionfish live on coral reefs in the Indian and Pacific Oceans.
fact: In the Atlantic and Caribbean, lionfish are an invasive species that eats many small fish, so divers catch them.
fact: In some places, lionfish are eaten as food.
exercise: What is a lionfish? | *A striped red, brown and white sea fish | A sea plant with big leaves | A small mammal that lives in trees | A bird with long wings
exercise: «Lionfish have venomous spines.» What does venomous mean? | Very long | Shiny and smooth | *Poisonous, able to sting | Soft and harmless
exercise: Why do divers catch lionfish in the Caribbean? | *Lionfish are an invasive species that eats many small fish | Lionfish are friendly and help divers | Lionfish can only live in cold water | Lionfish are rare and very cheap to buy
test: What does a lionfish with spread fins say to other animals? | It wants a friend | It is hungry | It is about to go to sleep | *Keep away, it can sting
test: Where has the lionfish spread, far from its home seas? | The Sahara desert | Only its home reefs | *The Atlantic and Caribbean | The Alps
exam: Why is a sting from a lionfish a problem for a diver? | The fish can fly out of the water | They help the diver swim faster | *Its venomous spines give a very painful sting | They are soft and safe to touch
